# Deploy pre-deploy migration gate manifest (scripts/deploy/write-migration-manifest.mjs):
# generated fresh from supabase/migrations at Docker build time, baked into the image, and
# never hand-edited or committed — a committed copy would silently go stale the moment a new
# migration lands without someone remembering to regenerate it.
/deploy/expected-migrations.json
test-output*.txt
# Downloaded staging tenancy CI artifacts are disposable; the one committed evidence
# document (run 29795051547) is a tracked repository file and must not be ignored.
docs/archive/staging-tenancy-evidence-*
!docs/archive/staging-tenancy-evidence-29795051547/

# Subagent-driven-development coordination: preserve durable SDD artifacts (ledger,
# briefs, reports, review packages) while ignoring ephemeral logs and scratch files.
.superpowers/*
!.superpowers/sdd/
.superpowers/sdd/**/*.log
.superpowers/sdd/**/scratch/

# Node compile cache written to a literal directory name.
# NODE_COMPILE_CACHE takes a directory PATH, not a boolean. A machine with it
# set to a bare value like `1` makes every Node tool - eslint, prettier, tsc,
# jiti - write `<value>/v<node>-<arch>-<hash>/` into the current working
# directory. Measured 2026-08-27: ~2,835 files / 20 MB per worktree, in a dozen
# of them. Ignoring it matters beyond tidiness: untracked, it inflates
# scripts/ci-change-scope.mjs with thousands of phantom changed files and forces
# every scope classification to the heaviest route.
# The real fix is to point the variable at a real path outside every repo. This
# rule is defence in depth for machines where that has not been done.
1/


# Scratch diagnostics written while investigating, never part of the suite. One is awaiting the
# owner approval the protected-work hook requires before it can be removed.
tests/zz-tmp-*.test.ts

# Clinical sign-off review packs, written locally by clinical:review / therapy:review --pack
sign-off-packs/
